# Cloudflare Pages _redirects — host-agnostic, applied AFTER Pages Functions
# (middleware) on both premiselabs.co and tortoise.premiselabs.co.
#
# 1) Trailing-slash variants: Cloudflare Pages serves a built-in 308
#    clean-URL redirect to the extensionless form; these explicit 301s
#    standardize the status code and target so every host/path variant
#    resolves identically to the canonical URL.
# 2) /index.html is the raw asset behind BOTH host roots — 301 to "/" so the
#    middleware root rewrite (company page / product page) owns the URL.
# 3) AUTH CONSOLIDATION: there is ONE auth page — /auth (301'd to the app
#    origin, app.premiselabs.co, where the `tortoise-dashboard` project owns
#    the BFF and the signup.html asset — see functions/_middleware.ts).
#    The legacy /signin URLs (and .html / trailing-slash variants) 301 to
#    /auth so the whole funnel (login buttons, dashboard/welcome redirects,
#    OAuth + recovery links, marketing CTAs) converges on a single screen.
#    /signup and its variants 301 straight to the app origin (the asset moved
#    there in #4054); the extensionless and .html forms are pinned because the
#    middleware only 301s them on the exact company host.

# /auth and the /auth/* subtree are owned by the middleware on every host (#4054
# for the page, #4346 for the endpoints): the page is a grandfathered 301 →
# app.premiselabs.co, the subtree is a 302 (SCOPE.md §12/F12 — a NEW branch for
# the moved surface is 302, never a 301). The middleware runs BEFORE this file,
# so a `/auth/` rule here would be unreachable; it is deliberately absent rather
# than left as a contradicting second copy. /signup, /welcome and /invite-accept
# moved with the BFF to the app origin and 301 there. /signin and its variants
# 301 to /auth — the old standalone login screen is gone. Trailing-slash variants
# are pinned 301s (the file's standardization contract; Pages' built-in 308s are
# not relied on):
/signup  https://app.premiselabs.co/signup  301
/signup/  https://app.premiselabs.co/signup  301
/signup.html  https://app.premiselabs.co/signup  301
/signin   /auth  301
/signin/  /auth  301
/signin.html  /auth  301
/welcome  https://app.premiselabs.co/welcome  301
/welcome/  https://app.premiselabs.co/welcome  301
/welcome.html  https://app.premiselabs.co/welcome  301
/invite-accept  https://app.premiselabs.co/invite-accept  301
/invite-accept/  https://app.premiselabs.co/invite-accept  301
/invite-accept.html  https://app.premiselabs.co/invite-accept  301

# Trailing-slash → canonical
/contact/  /contact  301
/privacy/  /privacy  301
/tos/      /tos      301
/license/  /license  301
/dpa/      /dpa      301
/security/ /security 301
/aviso-privacidad/  /aviso-privacidad  301
/docs/     /docs     301
/faq/      /faq      301
/self-hosted/  /self-hosted  301

# Raw index asset → host root (middleware rewrites / per host)
/index.html  /  301

# .html extension duplicates (non-auth only)
/contact.html  /contact  301
/docs.html  /docs          301
/faq.html   /faq           301
/self-hosted.html  /self-hosted  301
